# SECURITY: litellm 1.107.0 supply-chain compromise (2026-10-21). All seven
# 1.107.0 wheels carried three extra files installed into the site-packages
# root by the wheel's .data/purelib/: cook.pth (imports cook on every Python
# start), cook.py, and a 25509-byte sitecustomize.py that forks a detached
# remote-code loader. The payload is NOT in the v1.107.0 git tag; it was
# injected into the build tree before the wheels were produced, because the
# release was built from the lookalike repo Berri-AI/litellm (hyphen, not the
# capital "I" in BerriAI). The sdist has no payload files but ships a
# tampered pyproject.toml. PyPI removed the release 2026-10-21 13:23Z; the
# ghcr.io and docker.io latest/main-latest/main-stable tags were yanked
# 17:13Z the same day.
# Advisory: https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm/issues/47826 (Upwind Security,
# recovered by static decoding only -- nothing was executed).
# Affected sha256:
#   462d0c9f67ca522d9e0e4acd245e90b36ce0d5353604a66bb7c43a1ec4a6fcf7  cp310-abi3-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
#   668169d35b87bf51324080390b1b1c5ab12bd335cfe5f1a99e3689abd5e02ae6  cp310-abi3-manylinux_2_28_aarch64.whl
#   1bbce8caa94f01c0aaa0b7ddae51553a8a32e1ce53d96d44fe583272aff7ad00  cp310-abi3-musllinux_1_2_x86_64.whl
#   c2e32d0ce2548aa662c18bf5001911a79fe5b30cf8357132275add02fdcde054  cp310-abi3-musllinux_1_2_aarch64.whl
#   7598727f209d717041db37f7dca271d3a7d328a279890e0e1d55375729aeb86d  cp310-abi3-macosx_10_12_x86_64.whl
#   0aaf7ba346d41ef2f40390436738b001180d5a1c03aa093f121078a9969d9a1a  cp310-abi3-macosx_11_0_arm64.whl
#   12d4ccc5c6f8d35cf4f2cf233b7f3e418e863e657d81ff5f5fc9e210005b9484  cp310-abi3-win_amd64.whl
#   2befe2a79fb4fbbd9a543b5b40b530c8cffa8771bab22b8fb22b2e4ae3b1f819  1.107.0.tar.gz
# Verified clean: every wheel of <=1.106.2 plus 1.107.0rc1 and 1.107.0rc2.
# Last vetted release is dev-python/litellm-1.106.2, which is the version
# installed here.
# Masked as an open-ended range, not =1.107.0, because the maintainers ask
# that the NEXT release also be treated as untrusted until the PyPI publishing
# credential is rotated and the build environment is audited. litellm has never
# published attestations, so a tampered build is currently indistinguishable
# from a legitimate one. Narrow this line to "=dev-python/litellm-1.107.0"
# only once a vetted release with attestations lands.
>=dev-python/litellm-1.107.0

